course: dictionary
lesson: 13391
title: Heatedly and strong feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Heatedly is an adverb. An adverb tells you how someone does something. Here it tells you how people argued, talked, or shouted. «The two friends argued heatedly about who had won the game.» The friends were not calm and polite. Their feelings were strong and angry.
explain: Use the clues around the word. The words argued and shouting are the context, and they tell you the mood. Ask yourself: would someone in a calm, happy chat argue heatedly? No, so heatedly must mean in an angry, excited way with strong feelings. Check by swapping in your meaning: «They argued with strong, angry feelings about the game» still makes sense.
explain: Heatedly is about feelings, not just loud voices. Compare calmly, which means peacefully, with heatedly. A calm talk and a heated talk can be about the same thing, but the feelings are very different.
fact: Heatedly is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Heatedly» means in an angry, excited way, with strong feelings.
fact: It is often used for arguments and debates.
fact: It is linked to «heated», which describes an argument full of strong feelings.
fact: Context clue: if people are arguing, shouting, or disagreeing, heatedly is probably the word you need.
exercise: «The two friends argued heatedly about who had won the game.» What does heatedly mean? | In a sleepy way | *In an angry, excited way with strong feelings | In a calm and quiet way | In a silly, giggly way
exercise: In «The children argued heatedly, shouting over each other», which word is a clue that the mood was angry? | children | the | over | *shouting
exercise: Kai talked calmly and quietly about his plan. Is heatedly the right word to describe him? | *No, heatedly means angry and excited, not calm | No, heatedly means happy and giggly | Yes, heatedly means calm and quiet | Yes, heatedly means tired
test: «"No, that is my pen!" Sam shouted heatedly.» What does heatedly tell you about Sam? | *Sam was angry and full of strong feelings | Sam was happy and laughing | Sam was sleepy and bored | Sam was very quiet
test: The teachers discussed the new rules heatedly. What does the word heatedly tell you? | They were eating their lunch | They had forgotten the rules | They were relaxed and calm | *They had strong, angry feelings about the rules
exam: Which phrase best explains heatedly in «They argued heatedly about the match»? | very quietly | *with strong, angry feelings | without any feelings at all | slowly and carefully
